;; The VPN appliance with nothing to log into.
;;
;; feature:wireguard puts the driver and wg(8) in the image;
;; feature:wireguard-appliance is what makes it an appliance rather than a
;; box with WireGuard available — it generates a keypair on first boot, brings
;; up wg0 and prints the public key, because a machine with no login has no
;; other way to tell you its identity.
;;
;; The first boot of this image without that feature found something: the
;; password was locked, so login failed with "bad salt", but the prompt was
;; still there. BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_GETTY=n governs Buildroot's getty and not
;; systemd's, and no Kconfig symbol reaches serial-getty@.service.
;; profile:locked masks it now, in packs/locked, so every locked image is
;; locked rather than only this one.

(image qemu-arm-locked

  (compose
    target:qemu-aarch64-virt
    profile:locked
    feature:networking
    feature:wireguard
    feature:wireguard-appliance)

  (verified-against (buildroot "2025.02.16")))
